From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BananaDS <bananads@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] BananaDS: WFC settings kept, a DS MAC of its own per console,
 no states in local wireless play

- Platform::WriteFirmware saves wfcsettings.bin (2304 bytes, desktop melonDS's layout) atomically, so the WFC
  ID survives a restart.
- The DS MAC: wifi.mac, else the saved wifi-mac file, else the eMMC CID, wlan0's MAC or random, always
  00:09:BF and never changed once saved (kept for an existing wfcsettings.bin).
- In a local wireless game (Emu::mp_active) the menu greys out Save state, Load state and Restart, and the
  save/load hotkeys say why. Adds melonDS patch 0093 (the accessors it reads).
